<title>MEXICO: Breakdown of Mexico's 1997 budget.</title>
<headline>Breakdown of Mexico's 1997 budget.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Finance Ministry presented its 1997 budget proposal to Congress on Thursday.</p>
<p>Following are some of the ministry's projections for 1997 economic indicators and highlights of the government spending plan.</p>
<p>Economic indicator	  1996 estimate     1997 projection</p>
<p>Gross Domestic Product</p>
<p>    Real growth	     3.7 percent	  4.0 percent</p>
<p>    Nominal growth	  2,492.6 bln pesos  3,096.3 bln pesos</p>
<p>    GDP deflator	    34.1		   19.4</p>
<p>Average exchange rate     7.62 pesos/dollar     8.53 pesos/dollar</p>
<p>Inflation		     26.2 percent	 15.0 percent</p>
<p>Mimimum wage growth	 n/a		    17.0 percent</p>
<p>Price barrel of oil	 $18.05		 $14.50</p>
<p>Public balance (pct GDP)  0.0 pct		-0.5 pct</p>
<p>Current accounts	    -$1,014 bln	  -$4.300 bln</p>
<p>   As pct of GDP	    -0.31 pct	    -1.18 pct</p>
<p>**For the following budget items, the first number represents real cost in millions of pesos. The number in parenthesis is the percentage change from the year before.</p>
<p>Budget item		1996		   1997</p>
<p>Income		     560,726.3 (0.2)    694,900.6 (3.8)</p>
<p>  Federal gov't	  376,411.0 (0.4)    471,752.2 (4.9)</p>
<p>    Tax revenue	  214,581.1 (-5.8)   282,629.2 (10.3)</p>
<p>    Non-tax revenue    161,829.9 (10.1)   189,123.0 (-2.2)</p>
<p>  State enterprises    184,315.3 (-0.4)   223,148.4 (1.4)</p>
<p>    Pemex		   71,454.8 (8.5)     94,202.8 (10.4)</p>
<p>    Others		 112,860.5 (-5.3)   128,945.6 (-4.3)</p>
<p>Net payments	     562,246.8 (-0.3)   710,790.6 (5.8)</p>
<p>  Scheduled payments   391,874.7 (2.2)    491,693.8 (5.1)</p>
<p>    Deferred payments  -15,448.1 (n/a)    -14,999.0 (-18.7)</p>
<p>    Accrued expenses   407,322.8 (4.8)    506,692.8 (4.1)</p>
<p>Non-scheduled</p>
<p>	payments	   170,372.1 (-5.6)   219,096.8 (7.7)</p>
<p>    Interest		89,499.3 (-20.0)  119,693.6 (12.0)</p>
<p>State worker</p>
<p>	bonuses	     70,296.8 (6.9)     87,548.2 (4.3)</p>
<p>Liabilities from</p>
<p>    past budgets	  10,576.0 (n/a)     11,855.0 (-6.2)</p>
<p>Public-sector interest  89,966.3 (-19.9)  120,293.6 (11.9)</p>
<p>Primary budget surplus  89,048.8 (-21.4)  104,403.6 (-1.8)</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom, (525) 728-9507</p>
